WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
In 1517, a German
professor, Martin Luther,

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.780
challenged the sale of indulgences.

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.480
Printing presses spread
his ideas fast and cheaply.

4
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.820
Soon Western Christianity had split,
and Protestant churches multiplied.

5
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.570
You might expect a
split to weaken a faith.

6
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.790
So how did this one end up spreading
Christianity around the world?

7
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.800
In this mission, you'll compare what
Luther taught with the Catholic answer at

8
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.420
the Council of Trent.

9
00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.130
Then you'll see how Christian ideals
later shaped movements to end slavery and

10
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.080
to stand with the poor.

11
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:40.280
Your mission: find out how a split inside
Western Christianity spread the faith

12
00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.480
around the world.
